  {
   "text": "{\"sections\":[{\"section\":\"summary\",\"body\":\"Pellham Grain & Milling Co. is in breach of its Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio covenant for the period ended September 30, 2026. The bank calculated {{fact:3e25c14d-37d3-40d2-b995-7f155db348fd}} against a required {{fact:96526fb0-3f31-4d0a-a1ea-1eed755f60f1}}. The compliance certificate reports the same figure and does not claim compliance. Revenue rose from a year earlier while EBITDA, margin and net income declined. The breach has been decided for escalation to committee. The other two covenants are compliant, and the borrowing base agrees with the bank's records.\"},{\"section\":\"performance\",\"body\":\"Trailing twelve-month revenue rose to {{fact:365bc27f-9823-44b3-920a-82773a5c7c98}} from {{fact:ec309513-3385-4596-9a6d-fd4f392a5ccf}}, growth of {{fact:e7a41e90-73c4-459a-9759-1f1d0ee13897}}. EBITDA fell to {{fact:a18d02ea-49e0-4e5e-9945-d8e01604eff1}} from {{fact:fea29198-6279-42bf-a9e5-d70e32c3fc06}}, and margin narrowed to {{fact:cffc9381-9ebf-4995-b30f-a9cc90800faf}} from {{fact:92426544-d944-488c-a7af-dbdeb32685a1}}. Net income declined to {{fact:58258d72-9bc1-4e91-8697-97cc2a5b436b}} from {{fact:baf8d53f-5f62-437e-b84f-432947be73d6}}. Interest coverage improved to {{fact:224c9949-442a-400d-b379-4f91950fdea1}} from {{fact:7990b659-b48f-4b84-a5d1-b005d62ad9b7}}. The current ratio eased to {{fact:2fcdefdc-7ac9-4f11-8df2-a6d17466211f}} from {{fact:1d83f546-47d9-41d8-94d6-206d74310fe9}}. DSO moved to {{fact:e59cbad6-056f-4b02-8e7f-0eedae3dcf4b}} from {{fact:dba16fa7-d9d7-4325-935a-6e590cc60131}}, and DPO lengthened to {{fact:d9ef30f3-8789-4560-8ade-f3bd2a00d47b}} from {{fact:08f080f5-89fe-4fa4-bb2f-3f297fa01cac}}. Cash rose to {{fact:f8aaac9f-f084-4d2c-a86f-60f9a407961d}}, and total debt fell to {{fact:9a5073af-27df-4442-a9e2-36fc38144359}} from {{fact:3a32d08a-5634-46c1-a024-3741d338a41e}}.\"},{\"section\":\"covenants\",\"body\":\"The Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio is in breach. The bank calculated {{fact:3e25c14d-37d3-40d2-b995-7f155db348fd}} against a minimum of {{fact:96526fb0-3f31-4d0a-a1ea-1eed755f60f1}}, a cushion of {{fact:47368e5d-9530-498c-bb3f-6ccd8b1b8bf5}}. The certificate reports {{fact:70093d31-8e18-4b20-a9b5-90bc20f9d671}} and does not claim compliance. Minimum Tangible Net Worth is compliant at {{fact:1a32992e-9caf-4659-843e-e22961ab2bbe}} against {{fact:69ca664f-50a8-4689-b697-9a11045122d6}}, a cushion of {{fact:d4f98463-eb22-4247-955d-02db9ac098e4}}. Total Leverage is compliant at {{fact:876d6f53-2f65-4249-855a-9ab7e26ad582}} against a maximum of {{fact:fa0a3162-6f8d-4415-ace9-affa12fd0d5a}}, a cushion of {{fact:39f3c109-08b6-4908-941b-769f76f42a7c}}. Certificate figures match the bank's calculations for all three covenants.\"},{\"section\":\"collateral\",\"body\":\"The borrowing base supporting the Revolving Line of Credit, as of September 30, 2026, agrees with the bank's records with no mismatched lines. Availability is {{fact:8b594282-ec44-43de-84ee-46ffddd26a88}}.\"},{\"section\":\"risks\",\"body\":\"The Fixed Charge Coverage breach is the principal item. Its high-severity work item has been decided for escalation to committee. The covenant headroom signal fired at medium severity: coverage of {{fact:3e25c14d-37d3-40d2-b995-7f155db348fd}} sits below the required {{fact:96526fb0-3f31-4d0a-a1ea-1eed755f60f1}}, and no other signal fired. Interest coverage improved while fixed charge coverage fell short. A reviewer may wish to examine which fixed charge components drove the shortfall; those components are not among the facts held here. The decline in EBITDA and margin despite higher revenue also bears on future coverage.\"}]}",
   "type": "text"
  }
 ],
